# Astra AI Chatbot - local configuration
# This file is gitignored. NEVER commit real keys.
#
# HOW TO FILL: 
# 1. Copy this file to .env: copy .env.example to .env
# 2. Replace placeholder values with your actual keys/services
# 3. Leave lines commented (#) if you don't need that feature
# 4. Never share your real .env file
#
# Placeholder format: use CHANGE_ME or your_key_here
# Empty values = feature disabled (safe default)
# Never leave uncommented placeholder values in production

# ============================================================
# REQUIRED - chat / vision / speech-to-text
# Get one free: https://console.groq.com  -> API Keys
# ============================================================
# GROQ_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# (Uncomment and replace CHANGE_ME with your actual Groq API key)

# ============================================================
# OPTIONAL - uncomment (remove the '#') and paste to enable
# ============================================================

# Voice OUTPUT (text-to-speech). Without it, TTS returns 503 cleanly.
# Get one: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GEMINI_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME

# Live web search (Auto/Always toggle in the UI).
# Free tier: https://app.tavily.com
# TAVILY_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME

# Real RAG embeddings. Without it a local hash fallback is used automatically.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME

# Durable chat history. Without both, history lives in memory (per restart).
# SUPABASE_URL=CHANGE_ME
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=CHANGE_ME

# Code execution sandbox (Piston-compatible). Without it the Run button hides.
# ASTRA_SANDBOX_URL=CHANGE_ME
# ASTRA_SANDBOX_KEY=CHANGE_ME

# ============================================================
# TUNING - all have sane defaults, usually left alone
# ============================================================
# ASTRA_ROUTER_MODE=auto
# ASTRA_FAST_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# ASTRA_REASONING_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# ASTRA_VISION_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.8-27b
# ASTRA_STT_MODEL=whisper-large-v3-turbo
# ASTRA_MODEL_TIMEOUT=60
# ASTRA_STREAM_IDLE_TIMEOUT=30
# ASTRA_MAX_CONCURRENT_UPSTREAM=8
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=30
# ASTRA_STORE=memory
# ASTRA_SEARCH_PROVIDER=auto
# ASTRA_SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS=5
# ASTRA_EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER=auto
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# ============================================================
# FIRST-RUN INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================================

# Windows PowerShell:
# 1. Copy: Copy-Item .env.example .env
# 2. Edit: notepad .env
# 3. Fill: Replace CHANGE_ME with your actual keys
# 4. Run:  upsilon main:app --reload --port 8010
#
# Render.com:
# 1. Go to Render Dashboard → New Web Service
# 2. Connect your GitHub repository
# 3. Set the build command: python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
# 4. Set the start command: uvicorn main:app --port 8080
# 5. Add Environment variables in the Render dashboard:
#    - GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_key
#    - GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_key (optional)
#    - TAVILY_API_KEY=your_tavily_key (optional)
#    - SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_url (optional)
#    - SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key (optional)
#    - ASTRA_SANDBOX_URL=your_sandbox_url (optional)
# 6. Deploy → Service will restart with your configuration
#
# Important: 
# - The .env file is gitignored and never committed
# - All placeholder values (CHANGE_ME) are safe to commit in .env.example
# - Leaving values as CHANGE_ME or empty disables that feature safely
# - The app has sensible defaults for all optional integrations